#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166505 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166896 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "276898e7-57a4-5ca6-8df7-99fd318a2702" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Decoupled System of Linear ODEs"}] :question/id #uuid "a19f597d-f584-57b3-9e67-cb4cea07c876" :question/math-academy-id "e-21120" :question/problem "Which of the following systems of linear ODEs are decoupled?\n\n- ${\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=4{x}_{1}(t)+2{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)+6{x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}$\n\n- ${\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=-3{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=7{x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}$\n\n- ${\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=5{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}$" :question/worked-solution "A *decoupled system* consists of equations depending on only one variable, such as\n\n$$\nx'_i(t) = \\lambda_i x_i(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda_i$ is a constant. This means that we can solve each equation independently. \n\nWith this in mind, let's examine our systems.\n\n- System I is *not* decoupled because some of its equations depend on more than one variable. For example, $x'_1(t) = 4x_1(t) + 2x_2(t)$ depends on $x_1(t)$ and $x_2(t).$\n\n- System II is decoupled since its equations depend on only one variable each. Indeed, $x'_1(t) = -3x_1(t)$ depends on only $x_1(t)$ and $x'_2(t) = 7x_2(t)$ depends on only $x_2(t).$\n\n- System III is *not* decoupled because, for example, the first equation depends on $x_2(t).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166506 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166897 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ce35e5a9-2444-5e5f-9463-5a4d54496d9d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to a Decoupled Linear System of Differential Equations"}] :question/id #uuid "83ebd59d-883f-510a-9bc9-035b3088a43c" :question/math-academy-id "e-21123" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the system of differential equations given by\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=-6{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=3{x}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Given a decoupled system of first-order linear ODEs in the form\n\n![](images/17/17657d7db880fc0ababc24511039a9d7446952f7521e31ae3351adbb6b28ee61.png)\nthe formula for the general solution is\n![](images/44/44a286f1a4c15598038f38cdb4140534bac24caacb36f32ee4ef9cbe05b3e5e1.png)\n\nFirst, we write our differential equation in matrix form:\n\n![](images/d9/d9b9ac7fc20d076110f99476fc48d3c00c4206dc37fb2a929893fcbbb77d6526.png)\n\nSince the matrix of the differential system is diagonal, the system is decoupled. \n\nTherefore, the general solution is given by\n\n![](images/4f/4f7cfa979200fccf811a7e0d9a633b7919b33b7740c635a921b75ad09995e700.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166507 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166898 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cec0e48f-9fbb-5ada-b7fd-0d389d1b7438" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Initial Value Problem for a Decoupled Linear System of First-Order ODEs"}] :question/id #uuid "f5136df2-fcf6-5f64-aeda-f14a91231788" :question/math-academy-id "e-21124" :question/problem "Solve the initial value problem\n![](images/5c/5cc29f7492fded69b4100e10329c831cca0734a29966cd1aac2e8ad017636719.png)" :question/worked-solution "We have a decoupled system. Therefore, the general solution is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{1t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)t} \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{({e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(9)})}^{t} \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{9}^{t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find the values of $c_1$ and $c_2$ using the initial value $\\mathbf{x}(0).$ Substituting $t=0$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(0) & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{0}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{9}^{0} \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to our initial value problem is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =2[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+(-1)[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{9}^{t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]{9}^{t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304970 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166897 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ce35e5a9-2444-5e5f-9463-5a4d54496d9d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to a Decoupled Linear System of Differential Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01bf251b-dca8-56d7-a92a-48dd1eb46b6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t},\\,{c}_{1}\\in R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302461} {:answer/id #uuid "13696ed9-764e-541a-8b04-7b7e4287c673" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{10t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302584} {:answer/id #uuid "45ae77fa-b6af-5c75-b8a3-fa4d197cfa59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{10t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302896} {:answer/id #uuid "b263b137-d143-5ff8-a8a1-4f137bca92cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{5t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303560} {:answer/id #uuid "dc0e3b76-73a4-5a6b-914c-d61f970f4a36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t},\\,{c}_{1}\\in R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303828}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "45ae77fa-b6af-5c75-b8a3-fa4d197cfa59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{10t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302896} :answer-field/id #uuid "5d97aabb-32f0-532f-a52d-830e1ddabbe3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304331}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "69caff5b-f7ed-5470-8207-7540a07ed223" :question/math-academy-id "q-331989" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the matrix differential equation $\\,{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 10\\end{aligned}]x(t).$" :question/worked-solution "Given a decoupled system of first-order linear ODEs in the form\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }_{1} & 0 \\\\ 0 & {\\lambda }_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe formula for the general solution is\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nSince the matrix of our differential equation is diagonal, the system is decoupled. \n\nTherefore, the general solution is given by\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{10t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186391050 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166898 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cec0e48f-9fbb-5ada-b7fd-0d389d1b7438" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Initial Value Problem for a Decoupled Linear System of First-Order ODEs"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7e380f8b-d71f-55a2-ab1b-39f34cd89e65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-\\sqrt{5}t}+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]{e}^{8t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391052} {:answer/id #uuid "0f9827f0-71cf-5847-85bc-980bee16161f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{8t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391053} {:answer/id #uuid "ca29bc6f-4907-5a9b-91bf-39c3f6d764fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-\\sqrt{5}t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391054} {:answer/id #uuid "b312d8e4-025a-5e6d-99d6-bb6fe41ba80f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{8t}+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-\\sqrt{5}t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391055} {:answer/id #uuid "755f8ee4-1bac-5f8b-adc2-777c045fa529" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{8t}+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-\\sqrt{5}t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391056}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b312d8e4-025a-5e6d-99d6-bb6fe41ba80f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{8t}+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-\\sqrt{5}t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391055} :answer-field/id #uuid "6964b2cb-9fd8-5726-b5f5-384b2f89e701" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391051}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5620c47b-4e97-5ced-9381-5d5cc172acfd" :question/math-academy-id "q-332709" :question/problem "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}]x(t),\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We have a decoupled system. Therefore, the general solution is given by\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{8t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-\\sqrt{5}t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}$ using the initial condition $x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].$ Substituting $t=0$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(0) & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to our initial value problem is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =(-3)\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{8t}+6\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-\\sqrt{5}t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{8t}+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-\\sqrt{5}t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167314 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166897 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ce35e5a9-2444-5e5f-9463-5a4d54496d9d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to a Decoupled Linear System of Differential Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d9fa9552-b284-5ae3-90af-5c53bf0b2e49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t) = c_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}e^{\\sqrt{3}t} + c_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}e^{\\sqrt{2}t}, c_{1}, c_{2} ∈ R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165094} {:answer/id #uuid "01f1d4b2-8103-5f14-b4d1-1f6df9193ba8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t) = c_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}e^{\\sqrt{2}t} + c_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}e^{\\sqrt{3}t}, c_{1}, c_{2} ∈ R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165095} {:answer/id #uuid "1885614e-6511-5d68-89bb-33a23c4c4904" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t) = c_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}e^{\\sqrt{3}t}, c_{1} ∈ R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165096} {:answer/id #uuid "57253e72-5719-589e-86b0-abfcc7456d28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t) = c_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}e^{\\sqrt{3}t} + c_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}e^{2t}, c_{1}, c_{2} ∈ R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165097} {:answer/id #uuid "77ec0c39-01aa-537b-a144-1e5948502a91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t) = c_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}e^{\\sqrt{2}t}, c_{1} ∈ R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165098}] :answer-field/id #uuid "4af6f441-8de0-5fd3-8a85-5a544b462091" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165093}] :question/id #uuid "983f8128-2e0d-5ae8-ba5b-ec2151df4bcf" :question/math-academy-id "q-39026" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the system of differential equations\n${x_{1}^{′}(t) = \\sqrt{3}x_{1}(t); x_{2}^{′}(t) = \\sqrt{2}x_{2}(t)$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186392285 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166898 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cec0e48f-9fbb-5ada-b7fd-0d389d1b7438" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Initial Value Problem for a Decoupled Linear System of First-Order ODEs"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e9d9a47-3583-59c2-a4a5-d9b7cfbabc24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{\\sqrt{6}t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392287} {:answer/id #uuid "932c6061-7cb9-580f-acce-6047383bf69d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{6} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t}+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{\\sqrt{6}t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392288} {:answer/id #uuid "690d1f44-18ea-5111-91c1-cd804b8318f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t}+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{\\sqrt{6}t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392289} {:answer/id #uuid "3046ed62-20a1-55c9-81f9-f2e7be7aafa7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{\\sqrt{6}t}+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392290} {:answer/id #uuid "820e88f3-13a8-52c4-9120-9c26a28538cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{6} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{\\sqrt{6}t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392291}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e9d9a47-3583-59c2-a4a5-d9b7cfbabc24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{\\sqrt{6}t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392287} :answer-field/id #uuid "dbd8613b-a6de-5527-afe3-03ff9a9e544b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392286}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e6e051aa-62ce-5cb4-9eb2-83e2d1aaa8ea" :question/math-academy-id "q-39269" :question/problem "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{6} & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]x(t),\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We have a decoupled system. Therefore, the general solution is given by\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{\\sqrt{6}t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}$ using the initial condition $x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$ Substituting $t=0$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(0) & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to our initial value problem is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =2[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{\\sqrt{6}t}+0\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{\\sqrt{6}t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
